      "created": 1790516459612,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Module 17 — Trade-Off Thinking",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Module 17 — Trade-Off Thinking",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "87j4rWGEe7cM24PVsANuE",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 721.216145833333,
      "y": 4335.1981201171875,
      "width": 1073.5985107421875,
      "height": 180,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "am",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 526028013,
      "version": 1975,
      "versionNonce": 374633827,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790539103719,
      "created": 1790516585496,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Hard Constraint vs preference(Good To have) - Know what cannot be traded away\n2. Stronger vs Smaller Model - Match Capability to need\n3. More Retrieval - Balance Coverage and Noise.\n4. Single Agent or Multi agent(including critics) - Increase handoff handling and state and failure paths.\n5. Caching - Exchange repeated work for data freshness \n6. Autonomoy or Human Review - For simple task we can automate but for risky/complex/impactful workflow put HITL in place.\n7. Sync vs Async - Match interaction to Task Duration\n8. Shared vs isolated resources - Balance efficiency and isolation\n9. Reversibility and evidence - Explain when you would change your mind. (Though i feel it is a must have)",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Hard Constraint vs preference(Good To have) - Know what cannot be traded away\n2. Stronger vs Smaller Model - Match Capability to need\n3. More Retrieval - Balance Coverage and Noise.\n4. Single Agent or Multi agent(including critics) - Increase handoff handling and state and failure paths.\n5. Caching - Exchange repeated work for data freshness \n6. Autonomoy or Human Review - For simple task we can automate but for risky/complex/impactful workflow put HITL in place.\n7. Sync vs Async - Match interaction to Task Duration\n8. Shared vs isolated resources - Balance efficiency and isolation\n9. Reversibility and evidence - Explain when you would change your mind. (Though i feel it is a must have)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "UBnmWy-9skMpxrKPDQODS",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 772.4417012532549,
      "y": 3964.3358154296875,
      "width": 675.415771484375,
      "height": 35,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
